1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,900
I was sitting around,
just doing my thing,
When, all of a sudden,
I heard the bell ring.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,900
I opened the door
and who should I meet . . .

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,900
"Hi, I'm Zac,
I just moved to your street."

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,900
He asked for an egg,
in a nice polite way.
"Sure," I replied. "I just bought some today."

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,900
So I gave him an egg
and he laughed with delight.
And so he ran off
and was out of my sight.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,900
Zac returned moments later
—said "how do you do?"
He asked for some eggs—
but now he wants . . . two.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,900
I gave him two eggs, and he
soon skipped away.
(I hope it's the last time
I'll see him today.)

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,900
A little while later
he's back ringing the bell.
What was he up to?
I just couldn't tell.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,400
Again it was Zac,
won't he just let me be?
Now I'm giving him eggs—
this time he wants . . . three!

10
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,900
So I turned off the doorbell!

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,900
A few minutes later—
a knock at the door.
Zac says "I'm sorry",
but now he wants . . . four!

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,900
So I gave him four eggs,
'cause I'm nice that way.
And he looked very happy,
and just went away.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,400
The rest of the day
I just sat in my chair.
I kept checking the door,
but he wasn't there.
And in all of that time
he didn't come back.

14
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,900
I realized I missed him—
my new friend, Zac.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,900
At the end of the day,
when the sun had just set.
I still hadn't seen him;
I was kinda upset.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,900
I decided to check—
give it one last try . . .

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,900
And there he stood, with . . .

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,900
. . . a lemon meringue pie!

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:49,900
I brought him inside
for a warm cup of tea,
And we talked and we talked—
just Zac and me.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,900
He spoke of God's love and
His grace that was free,
And how Jesus died for
lost people like me.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:09,900
Now I felt very glad for the
things that Zac said,
And I thought of God's love
as I headed to bed.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,400
But one thing still bugged me,
I haven't a clue.
With all of those eggs,
just what did he do?

23
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,900
I thought and I thought,
then I understood why—

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,900
You need lots of eggs for . . .

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,900
. . . a lemon meringue pie!

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,900
But there's so much pie left!
We thought,
"What should we do?"

27
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,900
So we came round this morning
to share it with you!
